{\b\fs26\cf1 What's in Toasty}\par
Toasty shows your CPU, GPU and RAM temperatures and usage as colour-coded numbers in the system tray, with a pop-up panel for details, alerts and game sessions. Here is everything this installer puts on your PC, and why.\par

{\b\fs22 Toasty} \cf2(this app, MIT licence)\cf0\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\tx480\sa60\bullet\tab The tray app and panel, installed to Program Files.\par
\bullet\tab Runs as administrator, because reading temperatures needs low-level hardware access.\par
\bullet\tab Includes the .NET runtime (Microsoft, MIT), so nothing else needs installing.\par
\pard\sa100\par

{\b\fs22 PawnIO driver} \cf2(by namazso, GPL-2.0, optional)\cf0\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\tx480\sa60\bullet\tab A small, digitally signed Windows driver that lets apps read CPU temperature and power safely. It replaces the older WinRing0 driver that Windows Defender now blocks.\par
\bullet\tab Installed system-wide and shared with other monitoring tools that use it (e.g. LibreHardwareMonitor, FanControl). Skipped if already installed.\par
\bullet\tab You can untick it on the options page of this installer. Without it, CPU temperature shows as "-"; everything else still works.\par
\bullet\tab Uninstalling Toasty leaves PawnIO in place; remove it from Installed apps if you like.\par
\pard\sa100\par

{\b\fs22 PresentMon} \cf2(by Intel, MIT)\cf0\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\tx480\sa60\bullet\tab Used only while a game is being recorded, to measure FPS, 1% lows and stutter.\par
\bullet\tab Reads the frame timing events Windows already publishes. It doesn't inject anything into games.\par
\bullet\tab Can be switched off in Settings > Game sessions.\par
\pard\sa100\par

{\b\fs22 LibreHardwareMonitor} \cf2(MPL-2.0)\cf0\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\tx480\sa60\bullet\tab The open-source library Toasty uses to read sensors, built into Toasty.exe along with its helper libraries HidSharp (Apache-2.0) and DiskInfoToolkit / RAMSPDToolkit / BlackSharp (MPL-2.0).\par
\pard\sa100\par

{\b\fs26\cf1 Your privacy}\par
\pard\fi-240\li480\tx480\sa60\bullet\tab Toasty never connects to the internet: no accounts, no telemetry, no ads.\par
\bullet\tab Settings and game sessions are stored only on this PC, in %AppData%\\Toasty. You control how long sessions are kept and how much disk they may use.\par
\pard\sa100\par

{\b\fs26\cf1 Licences}\par
Toasty is free and open source under the MIT licence. Full third-party notices and licence texts are installed with the app (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the licenses folder), and the source code, including PawnIO's driver source, is published with each release.\par
